== 4.8 Chapter 4 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Evolution is best defined as],
  [the extinction of a species],
  [a change in an individual during its lifetime],
  [a change in the inherited characteristics of a population over generations],
  [any change in behaviour]
)

#mcq(2, [The mechanism of evolution proposed by Darwin is],
  [inheritance of acquired characteristics],
  [mutation pressure],
  [natural selection],
  [hybridisation]
)

#mcq(3, [Which of these is a fossil?],
  [A leaf on a tree],
  [A footprint preserved in rock],
  [A skeleton of a modern rat],
  [A living coelacanth]
)

#mcq(4, [Fossils are most often found in],
  [metamorphic rock],
  [sedimentary rock],
  [volcanic ash only],
  [igneous rock]
)

#mcq(5, [The oldest fossils are found],
  [in the top layer of rock],
  [anywhere in the rock],
  [in the bottom layer of rock],
  [in the middle layer]
)

#mcq(6, [*Archaeopteryx* is important as evidence for evolution because it],
  [shows features of both reptiles and birds],
  [is the oldest mammal],
  [has no feathers],
  [is a living fossil]
)

#mcq(7, [Structures with the same basic plan but different functions are],
  [mutant],
  [homologous],
  [vestigial],
  [analogous]
)

#mcq(8, [The wings of a bird and the wings of a butterfly are],
  [homologous],
  [vestigial],
  [analogous],
  [identical]
)

#mcq(9, [The human appendix is an example of],
  [a vestigial structure],
  [a homologous structure],
  [an acquired characteristic],
  [an analogous structure]
)

#mcq(10, [The forelimbs of a human, a bat and a whale are homologous because they],
  [have the same function],
  [are the same size],
  [contain the same bones in the same order],
  [are used in the same way]
)

#mcq(11, [The similarity of embryos of fish, reptiles, birds and mammals is evidence from],
  [fossils],
  [biochemistry],
  [biogeography],
  [embryology]
)

#mcq(12, [The fact that the same genetic code operates in almost every organism is evidence from],
  [fossils],
  [embryology],
  [comparative anatomy],
  [biochemistry]
)

#mcq(13, [Lamarck believed that],
  [species do not change],
  [all organisms are identical],
  [variation is random],
  [characteristics acquired during life are inherited]
)

#mcq(14, [Lamarck's theory was rejected mainly because],
  [natural selection is faster],
  [he did not believe in change],
  [acquired characteristics are not inherited],
  [he studied the wrong animals]
)

#mcq(15, [The giraffe's long neck is explained by Darwin as the result of],
  [stretching to reach high leaves],
  [the inheritance of acquired length],
  [a single mutation in one generation],
  [selection of individuals born with longer necks]
)

#mcq(16, [Natural selection acts directly on],
  [the phenotype],
  [the gene pool],
  [the genotype],
  [the chromosome number]
)

#mcq(17, [Competition in natural selection arises because],
  [all individuals are equal],
  [more offspring are produced than the habitat can support],
  [mutations are rare],
  [organisms cooperate]
)

#mcq(18, [The first step in natural selection is],
  [change],
  [speciation],
  [migration],
  [variation]
)

#mcq(19, [A new species forms most readily when populations are],
  [interbreeding freely],
  [geographically isolated],
  [of the same size],
  [in the same habitat]
)

#mcq(20, [Reproductive isolation means that two populations],
  [have the same genes],
  [are of different sizes],
  [can no longer interbreed to produce fertile offspring],
  [live in different places]
)

#mcq(21, [Which is a correct trend in the human fossil record?],
  [Posture became more bent],
  [Brain size increased and the jaw became smaller],
  [Teeth became larger],
  [Brain size decreased]
)

#mcq(22, [*Homo erectus* is known for],
  [having the smallest brain],
  [walking on all fours],
  [living only in trees],
  [using fire and tools]
)

#mcq(23, [Evidence that all living organisms share a common origin includes],
  [the same body size],
  [the same genetic code and similar proteins],
  [the same habitat],
  [the same number of chromosomes]
)

#mcq(24, [Which statement about evolution is correct?],
  [It happens in a single lifetime],
  [It explains the diversity of life],
  [It always leads to complexity],
  [It explains the origin of life]
)

#mcq(25, [The peppered moth in industrial England shows],
  [Lamarckian inheritance],
  [speciation],
  [natural selection within a human lifetime],
  [artificial selection]
)

#mcq(26, [Antibiotic resistance is an example of],
  [natural selection in bacteria],
  [neutral mutation only],
  [speciation in one step],
  [Lamarckian evolution]
)

#mcq(27, [Homologous structures differ from analogous structures in that homologous structures],
  [are always vestigial],
  [have a common function],
  [have a common origin],
  [are always the same size]
)

#mcq(28, [Vestigial structures are useful as evidence because they],
  [are fully functional],
  [are always harmful],
  [occur only in plants],
  [are reduced remnants of structures that worked in an ancestor]
)

#mcq(29, [A population of lizards is split by a new river. After many generations the two groups differ. This is],
  [speciation by isolation],
  [artificial selection],
  [convergent evolution],
  [acclimatisation]
)

#mcq(30, [Fossil evidence for evolution is limited because],
  [the fossil record is incomplete],
  [fossils are always complete],
  [fossils are easy to find],
  [fossils are all the same age]
)

