  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Evolution is a change in the gene pool of a population across generations.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Darwin's mechanism is natural selection acting on inherited variation.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A fossil is any preserved trace or remain of an organism that lived in the past.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Sedimentary layers bury and preserve remains, and their order records time.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The lower layer was deposited first, so it is the oldest.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It has feathers and wings like a bird but teeth, claws and a bony tail like a reptile.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Homologous structures point to a common ancestor.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    They do the same job with completely different structures, so they are analogous.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is a reduced structure that had a digestive function in an ancestor.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The bone plan — humerus, radius and ulna, carpals, digits — is shared.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Embryos pass through stages in which gill slits and a tail are visible in all of them.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Shared molecules and a shared code point to a shared origin.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    His theory of use and disuse required the inheritance of acquired characteristics.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Changes to the body or behaviour during life do not alter the gametes.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Long-necked variants reached more food and left more offspring.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Selection sees the phenotype; the genotype changes only as a consequence.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Limited food, space and mates mean that not all the young survive.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    There must be inherited variation before selection can act.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Isolation stops gene flow, so the two gene pools diverge.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    This is the point at which the two populations count as separate species.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Cranial capacity increased while the face and teeth became smaller.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Homo erectus was taller, had a larger brain, and used fire and stone tools.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Shared biochemistry is one of the strongest lines of evidence.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Evolution explains how life diversified, not how it first began.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Soot darkened the trunks, so the dark form was better camouflaged and increased.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The antibiotic selects the bacteria that already carry a resistance mutation.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Homology is about shared ancestry; analogy is about shared function.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    They make no sense except as reduced versions of once-useful structures.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Geographical isolation is the first step in the formation of two species.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
